<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43401" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐανδρ-ία</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>abundance of men</i>, esp. <i>of
				good men and true</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδὲ εὐ. ἐνἄλλῃ πόλει ὁμοία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Mem.</u>
					3.3.12
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				1.16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				16.2.13
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Per.</u>
				19
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>physical fitness</i>, as a subject of a contest, <i><span class="en">
				Din.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				16.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.956.48
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐανδρίᾳ νικᾶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					And.
					4.42
				</span></i>
			: so in pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ταῖς εὐανδρίαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ath.
					13.565f
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πληρωμάτων εὐανδρίαις</span>
			<i>by</i> the crews <i>being ablebodied men</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Pomp.</u>
				24
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>manliness</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>El.</u>
				367
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ δ᾽ εὐανδρία διδακτός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					913
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρασκευάζειν πρὸς
			εὐανδρίαν</span> to train to <i>manly spirit</i>,
				Antig.Rexap.<i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				7.7
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
